    <item>
      <title>Hello, World</title>
      <link>https://vetr0s.dev/articles/hello-world/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://vetr0s.dev/articles/hello-world/</guid>
      <category>meta</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This is the first published article under &lt;code&gt;/articles/&lt;/code&gt;. Every generator I have
used for this site starts the same way: a program that prints two words and
exits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Python&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;chroma language-python&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb&quot;&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;s&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;Hello, World&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bash&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;chroma language-bash&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb&quot;&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;s&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;Hello, World&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two languages, two runtimes, one output. That is as complicated as this post
gets.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
